      "evidence": "host = request.args.get('host', '')",
      "llm_reasoning": "The application only checks the length of the hostname but does not validate the content. An attacker could pass malicious characters even if shell=True is removed, potentially causing issues with downstream DNS resolution logic.",
      "suggested_fix": "Use a regex to validate that the host string conforms to standard hostname patterns (alphanumeric, dots, hyphens)."
